 "gpu": [
  "its former globals, function statics and lazily built tables are gone (lane/gpuenv, L2): per-environment state lives in struct env (csrc/engine/env.h), per-dimension state in the replay's dims, constant tables are built before main; csrc/tests/globals.sh lists what is left",
  "line 209, function fx_add: a layer at 4000 drops its oldest FX by a memmove of the array tail (container order is the spawn order)",
  "function particles_live_tick: FX spawned during the pass append to the array the loop walks (the bound pl->n grows), as the Java lists do",
  "function particles_live_init: EffectRenderer.rand is seeded from a constant, not the oracle's unrecoverable stream, so live hit particle positions differ by design",
  "struct particles_live holds 16000 FX inline (about 8 MB per instance)",
  "new_crit runs EntityCritFX's onUpdate through crit_update, not fx_update's dispatch, so the crit emitters' spawns do not re-enter fx_update"
 ],
 "tests": [
  "csrc/tests/test_rendertick.c",
  "csrc/tests/test_render.c"
 ],
 "notes": "lane/particles2 rebuilt it from the dig/explosion-only version: the base constructor now draws exactly the Entity constructor's streams (the old one drew one seeder long too many) and leaves prevPos at 0; getBrightnessForRender uses Block.func_149710_n (useNeighborBrightness) as World.getSkyBlockTypeBrightness does, not isOpaqueCube. Not ported: bubble, note, heart, cloud, snowshovel, blockcrack/blockdust, footstep, wake, fireworks, enchantmenttable, the villager particles, EntityPickupFX (a name without a class constructs nothing and spends no draws). The live client keeps the pinned minimal setting (2), under which only the specials and directly added FX exist. particles_live_pin (lane/clientrand) turns on Det's client consumer pin for the playable client: mrand, the FX's own Random and EffectRenderer.rand come from det_pin streams at client tick pin_t (the shared streams still drawn); the recorded scenes keep it off. lane/idxlast 2026-09-27: EntityNoteFX, EntityHeartFX (and angryVillager), EntityBlockDustFX as its own kind, mobSpell, mobSpellAmbient, witchMagic, snowballpoof and slime; rendertick fx_client."
}
